## Credit and Attribution

The MIT License already requires this, so it's worth stating plainly: any
copy, fork, or substantial portion of WinCore-Foundation you distribute —
modified or not — must keep the copyright notice and this license text
included with it. That's not optional and doesn't depend on this section.

Beyond that legal minimum, if WinCore-Foundation's code, a fused kernel, a diagnostic
approach, or any other part of this project ends up useful in your own
work, a mention of the WinCore-Foundation project and a link back to
https://github.com/FWKMultiverse/WinCore-Foundation.git — in your README,
credits page, or documentation — is genuinely appreciated. This part is a
request, not a requirement: the MIT License above does not obligate you to
publicly credit the project beyond keeping the notice in the source itself,
and nothing here changes that.

