## Project's Hope for How WinCore-Foundation Is Used

WinCore-Foundation was built as a practical, general-purpose tool to help people train
and ship PyTorch models on Windows more reliably — that's the problem it
exists to solve, and the hope is that it keeps being used that way: for
legitimate development, research, and production work that helps the
people using it.

This section is the project's own stated intent, nothing more. It does not
modify, restrict, revoke, or add any condition to the permissions the MIT
License grants above, and it creates no enforceable obligation on anyone
who uses, modifies, or distributes the Software. The MIT License's actual
terms are the only terms that govern use of WinCore-Foundation.
